WEBVTT

00:00.241 --> 00:03.746
You're already doing this job,
shipping pipelines, on-call, the

00:03.747 --> 00:08.250
works, but a few things slip past you
along the way, and you know exactly

00:08.253 --> 00:09.602
the feeling that I'm talking about.

00:10.099 --> 00:12.899
Sharpen is targeted, no starting over.

00:13.063 --> 00:18.126
It opens with a self-diagnostic against
ten gaps that trip up working engineers.

00:18.505 --> 00:22.140
Rate yourself one to five on
questions like, "Is overwrite

00:22.212 --> 00:23.524
ever your bronze strategy?

00:24.031 --> 00:26.702
Can you read a Spark UI and act on it?

00:27.034 --> 00:32.311
Do manual workspace changes survive in
your deployment?" Then eight pre-built

00:32.331 --> 00:34.855
bundles, and every unit stands alone.

00:35.258 --> 00:39.243
Want incremental and CDC so that you
could kill that full refresh habit?

00:39.585 --> 00:40.575
Go out and take that.

00:40.899 --> 00:43.674
Want data quality testing
and observability with

00:43.712 --> 00:45.643
quarantine and reconciliation?

00:46.072 --> 00:46.895
Go take that.

00:47.222 --> 00:51.152
Want modeling depth with
MDM and entity resolution?

00:51.503 --> 00:52.361
Then go take that.

00:52.713 --> 00:54.076
Nothing that you don't need.

00:54.447 --> 00:58.587
The weekly live review is there if
you want to pressure test anything

00:58.812 --> 01:03.740
because saying a decision out loud is
how you find out whether you actually

01:03.741 --> 01:05.310
are understanding what's going on.

01:05.854 --> 01:10.453
You get to come out sharper where it
counts with work that you could point to.

01:11.142 --> 01:14.636
Go run the diagnostic, see
what's missing, and let's fix it.
